<!--
  A representative shape of the feed at
  https://www.rotowire.com/rss/news.php?sport=NFL, kept here the way
  provider modules keep an `*.example.json` snapshot: as a reference for
  what the parser in `packages/core/src/news.ts` is reading.

  NOTE: this is hand-written to the documented RSS 2.0 shape, not a
  captured live response — outbound access to rotowire.com was blocked in
  the environment this feature was built in. Replace it with a real
  capture the first time someone runs an ingest against the live feed:

    curl -s "https://www.rotowire.com/rss/news.php?sport=NFL" \
      | head -c 8000 > apps/web/src/lib/news/rotowire-feed.example.xml

  The parser does not depend on this file; it handles RSS 2.0 and Atom,
  falls back to a body-text scan when a headline does not match the
  "Name - POS - TEAM:" shape below, and drops anything it cannot read.
-->
